      "mechanistic_theory": "WHAT FRA UNIQUELY COMPUTES. A head's pre-softmax score is a bilinear form on the residual stream: S^h[q,k] = (x_q W_Q^h)·(x_k W_K^h)/√d_h (row-vector convention; biases give pure row/column/constant terms). Substituting the SAE decomposition x_t = Σ_μ u^μ_t f_μ + e_t yields the EXACT partition S^h[q,k] = Σ_{μν} u^μ_q u^ν_k ω^h_{μν} + (feature×error) + (error×error) + bias terms, with ω^h_{μν} = (f_μ W_Q^h)·(f_ν W_K^h)/√d_h the weight-space pair coupling. Each (μ,ν) CELL is a multiplicative AND: its value is the product u^μ_q·u^ν_k, identically zero unless the query-content feature AND the key-content feature both fire (u ≥ 0 under ReLU/JumpReLU). This is the only exact additive decomposition in the attention pathway that lives in the JOINT (query-content × key-content) function space: the OV side (C^OV = A·u^λ·⟨f_λ W_OV, d⟩) is merely linear-given-pattern, and the post-softmax pattern admits no canonical decomposition (the denominator couples all cells across all keys — attribution needs the Jacobian ∂A_qk/∂s_qj = A_qk(1_{k=j}−A_qj), giving δT ≈ −u^μ_q u^ν_k ω_{μν}·g̃^h_{q,k} with the centered OV profile g̃^h_{q,j}=A^h_{qj}(g^h_j−ḡ^h_q); but the EDIT needs no linearization because it acts on s before the softmax). THE EDIT AND ITS EXPRESSIVE UNIQUENESS. The FRA edit subtracts c·u^μ_q u^ν_k ω^h_{μν} from ONE head's scores wherever the conjunction fires. With the SAE gates frozen it is exactly a support-gated rank-1 update of the head's bilinear form, ΔW^h_QK ∝ −c·ω_{μν}·e_μᵀe_ν restricted to {(q,k): u^μ_q>0 ∧ u^ν_k>0}; its only causal channel is that head's softmax → OV transport. A linear residual steer Δ (ActAdd/DoM/CAA/projection-removal), even gated by an ARBITRARY content gate g(x), is doubly weaker. (a) SCORE-SPACE EXPRESSIVITY: a gated query-side write changes scores by δs[q,k] = g(x_q)·(Δ W_Q^h)·(x_k W_K^h)ᵀ/√d, which varies over keys only through x_k's projection onto ONE fixed pullback direction v = Δ W_Q^h W_K^hᵀ. Cancelling a single cell requires ⟨x_k, v⟩ ∝ u^ν(x_k) for ALL k — impossible: u^ν is a thresholded nonlinearity of x_k, and even its linear part forces hitting the entire ν-ROW of the bilinear form plus every key cosine-close to v. A steer can imitate a row or a column of W_QK, never a cell; and (cycle-1 extension) FRA additionally supports SET ALGEBRA over cells — unions across heads/pairs and DIFFERENCES (differential cells = target-edge top-M minus sibling-edge top-M) — which no rank-constrained linear object in residual space can express at all. (b) RESIDUAL BROADCAST: the write Δ is deposited into the stream and read by EVERY consumer at the gated positions — all heads' Q, K AND V, the MLP, every later layer. Gating restricts WHERE the steer fires, never WHAT reads it. These two facts are the measured separability gap: at matched on-target removal a content-gated projection-removal steer strong enough to suppress the behavior destroys the content everywhere it legitimately appears (legit-content KL 1.77–2.64 nats), while the FRA cell-edit leaves it at ~0.000–0.0016 (≈1,000–26,000×), because legitimate occurrences fail the conjunction. THE MAGNITUDE LAW (validated in cycle 1): A ≈ reuse(marginal endpoint)/reuse(conjunction), with reuse measured ON THE EVAL/DEPLOYMENT SUPPORT, not naive corpus marginals (the s5 corpus-firing-rate operationalization is degenerate). Both extremes are now measured: A ~10³–10⁴× when the conjunction is unique (retrieval, acronym), and A→1.9× floor when a GENERIC endpoint makes the conjunction recur (shared-endpoint sibling test: a generic 'box-query' feature means (query × frog-value) recurs for the sibling, so FRA halves the sibling too). Corollary: selectivity is purchasable by differential cells (A 1.9→7.9× with sibling preserved) at a reach cost (on-target removal 58%→33%), because selectivity spends the score mass living in shared cells. NONLINEARITY LEDGER (what is exact where): RMSNorm is a frozen per-position SCALAR ×diag(γ) — it commutes into the activations u given the cached rms, so the score decomposition is exact on Gemma (edge-magnitude ratio 1.07 confirms). GPT-2 LayerNorm adds the fixed centering projector (I−11ᵀ/d); the ~50–75% edge-reconstruction shortfall is a LN-folding-convention artifact, not an FRA property; gold-standard hookpoint is ln1.hook_normalized but no public SAE suite ships it, and the grms check showed the hookpoint is not the limiter on RMSNorm models. RoPE is a per-position ROTATION applied AFTER projection: rotate each per-feature projected q/k vector, making the coupling relative-offset-indexed, ω^h_{μν}(q−k) = ((f_μ W_Q^h)R_q)·((f_ν W_K^h)R_k)ᵀ/√d (depends only on q−k by the block structure R_qR_kᵀ=R_{q−k}) — still exact per edge; the edit stays content-addressed with an offset-dependent coefficient. GPT-2's learned absolute positional embeddings enter simply as residual content (positional features → the CCF sink-mask handles them). Gemma's soft-cap s ↦ 50·tanh(s/50) is the ONE true nonlinearity between the bilinear sum and the softmax: cells are exact pre-cap, and an edit Δs reaches the pattern attenuated by tanh′(s/50) ≤ 1, so edits are compressed exactly on saturated edges. This — plus the SAE-unexplained score fraction (the error×· terms) and granularity×top-K fragmentation (1M-width SAEs split an edge across too many tiny cells for a fixed pair budget; 65k is the GemmaScope sweet spot) — is the complete account of FRA's suppression-reach ceiling. The ceiling bounds REACH, never separability: whatever FRA removes, it removes only on the conjunction's support. SUMMARY: FRA computes the exact joint query-content×key-content functional decomposition of attention selection, and hands you the corresponding cell-level (and cell-set-level) weight-edit whose causal support is a content conjunction — the missing middle between direction steers (marginal + broadcast) and position patches (specific but not content-addressed).",
      "bounds": {
        "win_checklist": [
          "1. EDGE-ROUTED (CCF-high): the behavior's proximate cause is pre-softmax score mass on identifiable attention edges, and that mass is dominated by non-sink content-feature × content-feature pairs after sink-masking (CCF reliable on gpt2; on gemma the current sink-mask over-kills late layers, so certify this clause behaviorally via LBNR). Kills positional/BOS edges (CCF=0.000) and output-direction behaviors with no score-space cause (weight-baked sleeper).",
          "2. LOAD-BEARING & NON-REDUNDANT (LBNR-R ≈ 1, measured BEHAVIORALLY with CAUSAL head-finding): cutting the identified feature-pair edge across ALL heads that carry it (heads ranked by causal edge-cut, never by raw attention — raw attention picks positional heads) removes the downstream behavior, and no backup circuit restores it. Kills IOI (R=−0.39, backups overcompensate), docstring (R=0.08), gemma knowledge-conflict (R=0.24).",
          "3. DIRECT CONSUMPTION: the behavior IS the edge's OV-transported content (the attended token's write into the output), not a downstream MLP computation that merely reads the attended info — so LBNR must be evaluated on the behavioral metric, not on attention or an intermediate. Kills greater-than (the > is MLP-computed; edge-cut dents behavior only 0.98→0.87).",
          "4. CONJUNCTION-SPECIFIC ON THE EVAL DISTRIBUTION (sharpened by cycle 1): at least one endpoint feature legitimately recurs in deployment (so every direction/content-gated steer pays collateral), while the specific conjunction does NOT recur legitimately — which requires the discriminating endpoint (usually the QUERY) to be TARGET-SPECIFIC, not a generic role feature; reuse must be measured on the eval-distribution support, not naive corpus firing rates (the s5 failure). If siblings share the value endpoint, differential cells (target-edge minus sibling-edge) must retain enough non-shared score mass to act on. Kills rare-dedicated-token triggers (a direction is already surgical, A→1) and generic-role-query setups (sibling A=1.9×).",
          "5. REACH (the only item bounding removal completeness rather than the win/lose verdict): the SAE-explained fraction of the edge score × head coverage × top-K pair budget — with granularity matched to K (65k GemmaScope sweet spot; 1M fragments at fixed K) — × soft-cap headroom tanh′(s/50) must clear the softmax margin on every carrying head at faithful scale c≈1–2, so a matched-removal operating point exists at which the separability comparison is defined."
