          "why_linear_steer_fails": "Moot — neither a linear steer NOR FRA cleanly addresses depth-matching, because the load-bearing variable (nesting depth) is an MLP-computed scalar count, not a residual direction OR a single attention cell. An FRA cell edit can only touch one opener-key while depth depends on the whole prefix.",
          "why_ranked": "Explicit LOSE control / dissociation experiment. Fails direct-consumption AND edge-routing: the matching DEPTH is an MLP-computed running count over a distributed bracket-detector, not a separable query-content×key-content product. The TYPE sub-component is the rank-5 win; this candidate's value is purely to draw the type-yes / depth-no boundary. Lowest importance, near-zero standalone win-probability — run only as the contrast to rank 5."
        }
      ],
      "shortlist_to_evaluate": [
        "Corpus-level selective copy-suppression release on natural OWT (gpt2-small L10H7 + negative-head union {L10H7,L11H10,L8H10}): both gates ALREADY measured (CCF 0.98, LBNR R=+0.95) — pure external-validity upgrade of a confirmed win. PROBE: causal negative-head ranking on a 100-token corpus pilot to gate union-cut fully clears suppression; then ablate (predict-X x earlier-X) cells on the union across ~10 target tokens spanning frequency deciles; on-target = logit(X) rise toward all-neg-heads-ablated oracle; collateral = corpus KL where X is NOT suppressed; A vs X-unembedding projection-removal at matched release. Reuses jobs/s3_copysupp_tier2.py.",
        "In-context PII regurgitation with sibling preservation (gemma-2-2b, ProPILE/DecodingTrust templates in the 2-needle harness): isomorphic to the confirmed ~1100x retrieval win, entity-specific query fixes the cycle-1 generic-query floor. PROBE: gate base P(first value token)>=0.2 on the record format FIRST; causal edge-cut LBNR on the Alice edge across top-5 heads; Tier-2 = legit-digit KL (dates/prices) + within-prompt Bob-extraction preservation vs value-direction projection-removal (jobs/retrieval_steer3.py) at matched extraction removal; differential cells (Alice-edge minus Bob-edge) if sibling overlap >30%.",
        "In-context NIAH entity-attribute retrieval with LEAVE-ONE-OUT transfer (gemma-2-2b, Wu 2024 retrieval-head harness): the novel content-addressed-transfer claim on the sparse no-backup retrieval circuit. PROBE: causal edge-cut LBNR confirming cliff-like no-backup failure; HEADLINE = extract the (entity-query x value-key) cell on haystack_0, apply unchanged to 3 held-out haystacks x 4 depths and measure P(value) drop vs a position-patch (fails when needle moves); decisive separability = KL on legit value sentences + authorized sibling-entity lookups vs projection-removal vs DeCoRe head-ablation. Reuses jobs/r2_fra_retrieval.py.",
        "NOVEL dual-use passage split — block verbatim regurgitation while preserving in-context QA (gpt2-small induction harness primary; gemma-2-2b QA-preservation arm): a capability no deployed mitigation can express, on the OWASP prompt-extraction threat; canary-uniqueness excludes the MLP-re-derivation failure. PROBE: enumerate carrying induction heads by causal edge-cut; cut the UNION of per-bigram cells over the passage swept over c; extraction rate (>=10-token verbatim) vs (a) QA accuracy over the same passage [gemma arm], (b) held-out-token KL; baselines = repetition penalty on passage tokens + passage-content projection-removal + induction-head ablation at matched extraction removal; stress arm = two vocab-sharing passages, cut A minus B (differential).",
        "Quote/delimiter-TYPE matching (gpt2-small, Gao et al. 2025 weight-sparse circuit): strongest STRUCTURAL LBNR prior — the type-matching head proven necessary+sufficient with direct-consumption by construction (OV copies the TYPE). PROBE: causal edge-cut of the type-T cell across edge-cut-ranked carrier heads -> P(correct closing type) for type-T drops to chance while other types unchanged, confirm NO backup restoration (the dense-model redundancy check); Tier-2 = legit-content KL on held-out matched type-T delimiters + a same-type in-prompt sibling pair, FRA vs type-direction projection-removal vs DoM at matched wrong-type rate. Reuses the induction cue-suppression harness.",
        "Knowledge-conflict counterfactual override on gpt2-small ONLY (Ortu et al. 2024 CounterFact): the gpt2-specific bet after the gemma twin already failed this campaign's LBNR (R=0.24); elicitation solved by construction (counterfactual wins 96%, fixing the base-rate trap). PROBE (gated): causal edge-cut of (final-query x counterfactual-key) across the L9H6/H9,L10H0/H10 cluster, require gap-flip R>=0.5 on the strong-elicitation domain subset; Tier-2 = legit-entity KL + a second authorized in-prompt lookup of the same entity vs entity-direction projection-removal at matched override removal; BONUS sign-flip arm (boost context-faithfulness, no baseline analog); pre-register differential cells if the copy-critique holds."
      ],
      "notes": "DEDUP: 25 brainstormed candidates consolidated to 17 distinct. Merged: (a) the 3 corpus-level copy-suppression variants -> rank 1; (b) the 3 gender-pronoun-stereotype variants -> rank 12; (c) the 2 knowledge-conflict/Ortu variants ('context-faithfulness knob' + 'counterfactual override') -> rank 6; (d) the 2 SVA-attractor variants -> rank 15.\n\nGROUNDING (read from CAMPAIGN_REPORT.md / SPRINT2_LOG.md / INCONTEXT_LOG.md + harness): CONFIRMED WINS this campaign = retrieval 2-needle (legit-KL 0.0016 vs steer 1.77 ~1100x, R=+0.63), acronym letter-movers (~26000x, R=0.95), copy-supp L10H7 single-prompt (CCF 0.98, R=+0.95). CONFIRMED FAILS/screen-outs = docstring (R=0.08), gemma knowledge-conflict (R=0.24, distributed), IOI (R=-0.39, backups overcompensate), binding (R=-0.89). DEFERRED on elicitation (mechanism passed, harness killed) = poison-RAG (R=+0.88 but base P=0.027) and gemma fact-recall (R=+0.86 but base P=0.039). These two deferrals are why ranks 6/9 (gpt2 knowledge-conflict, gpt2 fact-recall) score the way they do: same load-bearing mechanism, gpt2/model-correct-subset retry fixes the exact base-rate trap that killed the gemma versions.\n\nHARNESS IS MATURE (all reusable on one GPU): causal head-finding (g_screen, ranks by causal edge-cut NOT raw attention — raw picks positional heads); projection-removal steer fp16-safe (retrieval_steer3 gemma / acronym_steer3 gpt2) — NOT SAE-feature-subtraction (nan's on gemma, doesn't fire); differential-pair selection (shared_endpoint_diff); retrieval RH set baked (r2_fra_retrieval); copy-supp Tier-2 (s3_copysupp_tier2); random-repeated-token + IOI-backup probe (s2_lbnr). GUARD: A/legit-KL only valid at MATCHED on-target removal (confirm steer fires AND FRA suppresses).\n\nRANKING LOGIC: heaviest weight on CCF∧LBNR fit. Top of the list = where the mechanism is ALREADY measured load-bearing on infra that exists (copy-supp #1: both gates measured; PII/NIAH #2-3: isomorphic to the confirmed retrieval win on the sparse no-backup retrieval circuit). Mid = strong structural/published LBNR prior but un-banked or model-specific (quote-type #5: necessary+sufficient single head but from a weight-SPARSE model so dense-redundancy is the open risk; knowledge-conflict #6: published head-scaling flips behavior but relative-competition renormalization + copy-critique keep it uncertain). Parametric recall #9-10 = highest-value RETRY of an already-load-bearing screen-out, held uncertain by self-repair/MLP-enriched-key/redundancy. DOWN-RANKED HARD: gender-stereotype #12 (highest importance + beats the field's own INLP baseline, but the mechanism IS the IOI name-mover family that failed LBNR + Mathwin's MLP-interposed multi-hop graph -> uncertain-tending-fail; gender is also a residual direction); poison-RAG #13 (dominated by PII/NIAH — same retrieval story, cleaner elicitation, and the scaffold-fix risks migrating to a distributed direction). EXPLICIT LOSE CONTROLS at the bottom: SVA #15 (MLP-computed morphology + distributed + positional attention — fails 3 clauses), WinoBias Type-1 #16 (IOI backups, R<=0), Dyck-depth #17 (MLP-counted depth, not a cell). gemma copy-supp #14 sits low because McDougall's own paper pre-warns no clean analog exists in larger models + gemma sink-mask breaks CCF.\n\nSHORTLIST RATIONALE (6, priority order): #1 copy-supp-corpus is the safest near-certain win (gates measured, infra exists). #2 PII + #3 NIAH are the two highest-importance deployment wins riding the strongest confirmed mechanism (retrieval, sparse/no-backup) with the entity-specific query that fixes the cycle-1 generic-query floor — both gate on gemma-base elicitation (base P>=0.2) which is the one real risk and is cheap to check first. #4 dual-use passage split is the most novel + most publication-shaped (a capability no mitigation can express) with canary-uniqueness rigorously excluding the MLP/weight-baked failure modes. #5 quote-type has the cleanest possible structural LBNR (necessary+sufficient + direct-consumption by construction) on a fresh benchmark — the dense-redundancy check is the whole experiment. #6 gpt2 knowledge-conflict is the highest-value model-specific retry: the gemma twin failed LBNR but gpt2 has published head-causality AND solves the elicitation trap by construction; gated hard on R>=0.5, with the unique sign-flip arm as bonus. All 6 run NOW on gpt2-small/gemma-2-2b with existing harness; the only new code per candidate is a prompt builder + metric. Deliberately EXCLUDED from the shortlist despite high importance: gender-stereotype (run the cheap gpt2 LBNR screen as a side-experiment — a clean fail is a publishable taxonomy negative — but don't commit Tier-2 until R>=0.6 with coref accuracy preserved) and the explicit LOSE controls (SVA, WinoBias-1, Dyck — run cheap to calibrate the screen, not as wins)."
    }
  }
}